  :""lower_language_def""
  <latex>\rightarrow \texttt{rhoapi::Par}</latex> scalar contracts;<<#DCFCE7>>
  :""rho_net_*"" driver network
  + interned set-automaton pattern DAG
  <latex>\rightarrow \texttt{rhoapi::Par}</latex>;<<#DCFCE7>>
  :""NativeHandlerSpec"" table
  <latex>\rightarrow</latex> system-process ""Definition""s,
  injected via ""extra_system_processes"";<<#DCFCE7>>
  note right
    **Already data.** A running node can install all of this
    from a specification value with no compiler in the loop.
    The crate's own documentation says so:
    <i>lower_language_def emits normalized Rholang AST</i>
    <i>(rhoapi::Par) for the supported native scalar subset …</i>
    <i>and keeps Rholang-looking text only as a</i>
    <i>reader/debug annotation.</i>
    — rholang-codegen/src/lib.rs module documentation
  end note
  :**installed with NO compile step**;<<#BFDBFE>>
split again
  |Syntax lane — emits RUST SOURCE|
  :PraTTaIL / WPDA pipeline ""run_pipeline""
  <latex>\rightarrow</latex> a ""String"" of Rust source, then
  ""combined.parse::<TokenStream>()"";<<#FEE2E2>>
  :AST enums, freshness fns, metadata,
  ""Language"" impl, proptest strategies,
  test / simulator / Blockly emitters;<<#FEE2E2>>
  :""rustc"";<<#FCA5A5>>
  note right
    **Still code.** ""run_pipeline""'s terminal step is a
    ""parse::<TokenStream>()"" over concatenated Rust source
    (prattail/src/pipeline/state.rs::run_pipeline_with_analysis).
    Obtaining a //parser// for a language authored at runtime is
    the one genuinely missing artifact — work item **W-4**,
    serializable WPDA tables walked by the existing ""WpdaWalker"".
  end note
  :installed **only after a compile step**;<<#BFDBFE>>
